---
import Card from "./Card.astro";
import Label from "./Label.astro";
---

<section id="safety" class="border-b border-neutral-950 py-20 sm:py-28">
	<Label tone="alert">02 / Paranoid safety</Label>
	<h2
		class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-5xl"
	>
		Two rules uppy enforces no matter what your config says.
	</h2>
	<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-neutral-700">
		Renovate makes these optional. uppy makes them non-negotiable — if your
		config asks for less, uppy ignores it.
	</p>

	<div class="mt-12 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
		<Card
			kicker="Minimum release age"
			title="A 3-day floor, always"
			tone="alert"
		>
			<p>
				uppy will not recommend a version until it has been published for at
				least three days. Set a shorter cooldown in config and it makes no
				difference — the paranoid floor wins. Time in the wild is the cheapest
				safety check there is, so uppy never skips it.
			</p>
		</Card>

		<Card
			kicker="Digest pinning"
			title="The sha is the ground truth"
			tone="alert"
		>
			<p>
				Every unpinned GitHub Action gets pinned to the exact commit sha its tag
				resolves to — <code class="font-mono text-neutral-950"
					>@&lt;sha&gt; # v4.1.0</code
				>. The trailing comment is attacker-controllable, so uppy never trusts
				it: it reverse-resolves the sha to a tag, because the sha is what GitHub
				actually checks out.
			</p>
		</Card>
	</div>
</section>
